node_modules
dist
coverage

# TypeScript incremental build cache. `dist` above does not cover it — tsc puts
# it at the project root once `rootDir` is pinned. Copying a developer's or a
# deploy host's stale cache into the build context makes the in-image
# `yarn build` emit nothing while still exiting 0, producing an image with no
# application code. `git reset --hard` on a deploy host does not remove
# untracked files, so one left behind there would poison every later build.
# `**/` because Docker ignore patterns are path-segment-scoped and a bare `*`
# would not match a nested cache.
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.idea
.vscode
**/*.log
test
README.md
CLAUDE.md
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.prettierrc
eslint.config.mjs
